1
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:14,500
Quand ils sont arrivés, il n'y avait pas de doute que j'étais la seule.
When they arrived, there was no doubt I was the only one.

2
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:17,540
Oui, mais vous savez qu'ils mentent.
Yes, but you know they're lying.

3
00:00:18,770 --> 00:00:22,230
Non, non, non, je ne veux pas négocier avec eux, je veux qu'ils paient pour ce qu'ils ont fait.
No, no, no, I don't want to negotiate with them, I want them to pay for what they did.

4
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:24,330
Oui.
Yes.

5
00:00:25,430 --> 00:00:26,630
D'accord, vous m'appellez, merci.
Alright, call me, thank you.

6
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:29,360
Alors, il dit quoi, ton avocat ?
So, what does your lawyer say?

7
00:00:29,360 --> 00:00:31,940
Il dit que ça sent pas bon, UBA est en train d'essayer de prouver
He says it doesn't look good — UBA is trying to prove

8
00:00:31,940 --> 00:00:33,860
que j'étais pas la seule candidate pour le poste à New York.
that I wasn't the only candidate for the New York position.

9
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:36,840
C'est pas vrai, c'est quand tu leur as dit que t'étais enceinte qu'ils ont eu la proposition.
That's not true, it was when you told them you were pregnant that they withdrew the offer.

10
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:41,020
Oui, sauf que si l'agence UBA arrive à prouver que j'étais pas la seule candidate pour le poste,
Yes, except that if UBA manages to prove I wasn't the only candidate for the position,

11
00:00:41,020 --> 00:00:42,860
alors il n'y a plus de discrimination à l'embauche.
then there's no more hiring discrimination.

12
00:00:43,020 --> 00:00:45,060
Tu vois, c'est juste une banale concurrence.
You see, it's just ordinary competition.

13
00:00:45,160 --> 00:00:45,840
On va gagner.
We're going to win.

14
00:00:46,560 --> 00:00:48,120
Tu sais pourquoi ? Regarde.
You know why? Look.

15
00:00:49,120 --> 00:00:49,500
Quoi ?
What?

16
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:50,380
Laisse ta main, regarde.
Give me your hand, look.

17
00:00:51,390 --> 00:00:54,410
Oh, mais non, mais je l'avais pas vue.
Oh, no way, I hadn't seen that.

18
00:00:55,570 --> 00:00:56,730
Attends, elle fait un doigt d'honneur.
Wait, she's giving the finger.

19
00:00:58,060 --> 00:01:00,180
Non, mais attends, elle démonte notre fille.
No, but wait — she's roasting our daughter.

20
00:01:00,440 --> 00:01:00,980
S'il vous plaît.
Please.

21
00:01:10,660 --> 00:01:10,980
Merci.
Thank you.

22
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:11,920
Merci de passer un écueil.
Thank you for getting past that hurdle.

23
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:15,520
On est bien prêts.
We're all set.

24
00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:19,510
Bah, d'habitude, t'adores les choquettes.
Come on, you usually love cream puffs.

25
00:01:19,750 --> 00:01:22,230
Non, mais j'ai pas faim, c'est ce bilan de fin d'année qui arrive, ça me stresse.
No, I'm just not hungry — it's this year-end review coming up, it's stressing me out.

26
00:01:22,830 --> 00:01:24,650
Je te rassure, ma cocotte, le bilan de fin d'année,
Don't worry, sweetheart, the year-end review

27
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:25,450
ça stresse tout le monde.
stresses everyone out.

28
00:01:25,630 --> 00:01:27,930
Moi, j'ai signé que cinq contrats depuis que je suis agent.
I've only signed five contracts since I became an agent.

29
00:01:28,110 --> 00:01:29,370
Je pense que Richard va me lâcher.
I think Richard is going to drop me.

30
00:01:29,770 --> 00:01:32,550
Ça, quand tu deviens agent, il faut avoir les épaules pour encaisser la pression.
Look, when you become an agent, you have to have tough shoulders to handle the pressure.

31
00:01:32,630 --> 00:01:33,630
Il y en a qui explosent en plein vol.
Some people crash and burn.

32
00:01:33,930 --> 00:01:35,090
Ça va, toi, la punaise.
Easy there, genius.

33
00:01:37,540 --> 00:01:39,420
C'est arrivé, le coursier, avec le contrat du jardin ?
Has the courier shown up yet with the garden contract?

34
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:39,760
Euh, non.
Uh, no.

35
00:01:40,080 --> 00:01:40,940
C'est chiant.
That's annoying.

36
00:01:42,290 --> 00:01:43,010
Salut, la compta.
Hey, accounting.

37
00:01:43,310 --> 00:01:45,850
Dis, Jean-Pierre, la clôture des comptes pour le bilan de fin d'année,
Hey Jean-Pierre, the account closing for the year-end review —

38
00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:46,770
c'est quand exactement ?
when exactly is that?

39
00:01:46,770 --> 00:01:47,150
Vendredi.
Friday.

40
00:01:47,670 --> 00:01:49,130
Ce vendredi-là, dans quatre jours ?
This Friday? In four days?

41
00:01:49,130 --> 00:01:50,270
C'est tendu.
That's tight.

42
00:01:50,570 --> 00:01:54,490
Donc, tout contrat signé avant vendredi fait bien partie des comptes de l'année ?
So any contract signed before Friday counts toward this year's figures?

43
00:01:54,490 --> 00:01:54,890
Exact.
Correct.

44
00:01:54,890 --> 00:01:55,790
OK, cool.
OK, great.

45
00:01:57,050 --> 00:01:58,290
Il a fait combien, Mathias ?
How much did Mathias bring in?

46
00:01:58,690 --> 00:02:00,830
Ça, c'est une information que je ne peux certainement pas te donner.
That is information I most certainly cannot share with you.

47
00:02:01,390 --> 00:02:02,290
Je sais, mon Jean-Pierre.
I know, my dear Jean-Pierre.

48
00:02:02,730 --> 00:02:03,530
Je te fais marcher.
I'm just messing with you.

49
00:02:04,010 --> 00:02:05,430
Je m'en fous, en plus, de ce qu'a fait Mathias.
Besides, I couldn't care less what Mathias did.

50
00:02:09,120 --> 00:02:09,760
Ça va ?
You okay?

51
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:12,190
T'es sûre ?
You sure?

52
00:02:13,350 --> 00:02:15,430
C'est juste que, ouais, des fois, j'ai des contractions.
It's just that, yeah, sometimes I get contractions.

53
00:02:15,550 --> 00:02:17,570
Je veux bien, peut-être, juste un verre d'eau.
I'd love maybe just a glass of water.

54
00:02:17,610 --> 00:02:17,890
Assieds-toi.
Sit down.

55
00:02:18,070 --> 00:02:19,330
Je reviens tout de suite.
I'll be right back.

56
00:02:19,470 --> 00:02:19,870
Ouais, super.
Yeah, great.

57
00:02:37,310 --> 00:02:38,270
C'est bon, c'est passé.
It's fine, it passed.

58
00:02:51,020 --> 00:02:52,600
Je peux me réveiller, là ?
Can I wake up now?

59
00:02:52,600 --> 00:02:54,840
Peut-être que j'en reviens toujours pas, que toi, tu sois enceinte.
I still can't get over the fact that you're pregnant.

60
00:02:55,220 --> 00:02:55,900
Ouais, moi non plus.
Yeah, me neither.

61
00:02:57,540 --> 00:02:59,220
Ouais, c'est pas une raison pas de te reposer, là.
Yeah, that's no reason not to get some rest, though.

62
00:03:01,040 --> 00:03:02,460
Au fait, Andréa, je voulais te demander,
By the way, Andrea, I wanted to ask you,

63
00:03:02,680 --> 00:03:05,400
j'ai une copine lesbienne qui voudrait vraiment avoir un enfant
I have a lesbian friend who really wants to have a child

64
00:03:05,400 --> 00:03:06,740
et elle aurait besoin de renseignements.
and she'd need some information.

65
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:09,100
Tu pourrais dire comment t'as procédé, toi ?
Could you explain how you went about it?

66
00:03:09,100 --> 00:03:10,900
T'as fait appel à un donneur ?
Did you use a donor?

67
00:03:10,900 --> 00:03:13,560
Je te demande, toi, si tu mets un stérilet ou un implant contraceptif.
I'm asking you whether you use an IUD or a contraceptive implant.

68
00:03:13,720 --> 00:03:14,860
Non, non, j'ai un besoin d'un martel.
No, no, I need a hammer.

69
00:03:15,420 --> 00:03:15,980
Pour moi ?
For me?

70
00:03:15,980 --> 00:03:16,880
C'est moi ?
Is that me?

71
00:03:25,290 --> 00:03:27,050
Le deal pour Guillaume Canet, ça y est, c'est fait.
The deal for Guillaume Canet — it's done, it's signed.

72
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,820
Je dois te dire que je suis assez content.
I have to say I'm pretty pleased.

73
00:03:29,280 --> 00:03:30,320
Enfin, surtout pour mon client.
Well, mostly for my client.

74
00:03:31,270 --> 00:03:32,990
Guillaume m'a appelé ce matin pour me remercier.
Guillaume called me this morning to thank me.

75
00:03:32,990 --> 00:03:35,550
C'est vrai qu'un contrat comme ça, on le signe pas tous les jours.
It's true that you don't sign a contract like that every day.

76
00:03:35,770 --> 00:03:37,810
Hé, mais méfie-toi, tu vas faire de l'ombre à tes collègues.
Hey, watch out — you're going to overshadow your colleagues.

77
00:03:38,810 --> 00:03:40,570
Tu sais, ils ont l'habitude, ça fait dix ans
They're used to it, trust me — it's been ten years

78
00:03:40,570 --> 00:03:42,090
que j'ai toujours le meilleur chiffre d'affaires de l'agence.
since I've had the highest revenue in the agency.

79
00:03:43,670 --> 00:03:45,350
Ouais, sauf qu'un du jardin égale deux Canets.
Yeah, except one from the garden deal equals two Canets.

80
00:03:45,810 --> 00:03:48,150
C'est le contrat du jardin, signé, de sa main.
It's the garden contract, signed, in his own hand.

81
00:03:48,950 --> 00:03:51,590
Quelque chose me dit que, cette année, c'est moi qui vais faire le plus gros chiffre.
Something tells me that this year, I'll be the one posting the biggest numbers.

82
00:03:52,010 --> 00:03:52,710
Salut, les mecs.
Hey, guys.

83
00:03:53,550 --> 00:04:23,410
Le B, le B, c'est quoi, ce B ?
The B, the B — what's this B?

84
00:04:26,980 --> 00:04:27,540
Émile Berthier.
Émile Berthier.

85
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:14,640
Le téléphone de Jean est coupé, celui de sa femme répond pas non plus.
Jean's phone is off, his wife's isn't picking up either.

86
00:05:15,570 --> 00:05:16,810
Peut-être qu'il a voulu faire une blague.
Maybe he wanted to play a joke.

87
00:05:16,970 --> 00:05:17,490
Une blague ?
A joke?

88
00:05:17,790 --> 00:05:20,250
Jean a énormément d'humour, mais c'est un truc avec lequel il rigole pas,
Jean has a great sense of humor, but there's one thing he never jokes about —

89
00:05:20,330 --> 00:05:21,410
c'est ses contrats, sur tout son montant.
his contracts, down to every last cent.

90
00:05:21,530 --> 00:05:23,250
T'es sûre qu'il est pas encore sur le tournage du Déserteur ?
Are you sure he's not still on the set of Le Déserteur?

91
00:05:23,250 --> 00:05:25,010
Oui, j'ai vérifié, il a fini il y a deux semaines.
Yes, I checked — he wrapped two weeks ago.

92
00:05:25,470 --> 00:05:27,450
Putain, c'est pas vrai, qu'est-ce qu'il fout ?
For God's sake, what the hell is he up to?

93
00:05:27,450 --> 00:05:27,970
Je sais pas.
I don't know.

94
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,280
Un problème avec Jean Dujardin, peut-être ?
A problem with Jean Dujardin, maybe?

95
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,400
Non, pas de problème avec Jean Dujardin.
No, no problem with Jean Dujardin.

96
00:05:31,460 --> 00:05:32,780
Tu peux fermer la porte, s'il te plaît, Mathieu, parce que...
Can you close the door, please, Mathieu, because…

97
00:05:34,390 --> 00:05:34,630
Merci.
Thank you.

98
00:05:41,050 --> 00:05:41,790
Bah, tu vas nettoyer.
Well, you're going to clean it.

99
00:05:41,970 --> 00:05:43,010
Non, ça, c'est pas possible.
No, that's not possible.

100
00:05:43,290 --> 00:05:45,170
En fait, il y a 2000 pages moisies qui puent la bête morte.
There are literally 2,000 pages, moldy and reeking of something dead.

101
00:05:45,170 --> 00:05:47,170
Je m'en fous, rendez-vous tout à l'heure avec la productrice,
I don't care — I have a meeting with the producer later,

102
00:05:47,210 --> 00:05:48,110
je vais lui remettre le contrat en main propre.
I'm going to hand her the contract in person.

103
00:05:48,770 --> 00:05:51,110
Je sais pas, tu vas au BHB, tu cherches un produit qui lave le papier,
I don't know, go to BHB, find something that cleans paper,

104
00:05:51,230 --> 00:05:51,510
tu te démerdes.
figure it out.

105
00:05:51,570 --> 00:05:53,010
Ça n'existe pas, un produit qui lave le papier.
There's no such thing as a product that cleans paper.

106
00:05:53,410 --> 00:05:54,010
T'en sais rien.
You don't know that.

107
00:05:54,790 --> 00:05:56,770
Et pour la signature Émile Berthier, tu vas dire quoi ?
And about the Émile Berthier signature — what are you going to say?

108
00:05:56,770 --> 00:05:58,110
Qu'il a repris son nom de jeune fille ?
That he took back his maiden name?

109
00:05:58,630 --> 00:05:58,910
Arrête.
Stop.

110
00:05:59,330 --> 00:06:00,850
Arrête de faire ta maligne parce que t'es devenu agent.
Stop acting clever just because you became an agent.

111
00:06:01,690 --> 00:06:01,970
Andrea.
Andrea.

112
00:06:02,310 --> 00:06:02,690
Oui ?
Yes?

113
00:06:02,690 --> 00:06:03,570
Ton rendez-vous est arrivé.
Your appointment is here.

114
00:06:04,030 --> 00:06:05,310
Bonjour, Andrea.
Hello, Andrea.

115
00:06:06,170 --> 00:06:08,110
Bah, bête, comment ça va ?
Hey, sweetie, how are you?

116
00:06:08,630 --> 00:06:09,230
Bien, bien.
Good, good.

117
00:06:09,470 --> 00:06:11,570
Je passe juste un coup de vent à récupérer le contrat de Jean.
I'm just stopping by quickly to pick up Jean's contract.

118
00:06:11,710 --> 00:06:12,950
T'as pas eu mon message ?
Didn't you get my message?

119
00:06:13,510 --> 00:06:13,790
Non.
No.

120
00:06:14,390 --> 00:06:14,890
Ah bon ?
Really?

121
00:06:14,890 --> 00:06:17,090
Ah non, mais c'est de notre faute, c'est le service juridique.
No, no, it's our fault — it's the legal department.

122
00:06:17,690 --> 00:06:18,950
Ils ont pas envoyé la bonne version.
They didn't send the right version.

123
00:06:19,330 --> 00:06:21,110
Donc ça y est, on a renvoyé un exemplaire du contrat,
So we've resent a copy of the contract,

124
00:06:21,190 --> 00:06:22,170
donc on l'aura ce soir.
so we'll have it tonight.

125
00:06:22,310 --> 00:06:23,410
Max, t'inquiète.
Max, don't worry.

126
00:06:23,810 --> 00:06:24,910
Mais ça me fait plaisir de te voir.
But it's so good to see you.

127
00:06:25,670 --> 00:06:26,090
Coucou, toi.
Hey, you.

128
00:06:26,250 --> 00:06:27,950
Comment il s'appelle, déjà, ce petit coquin ?
What's his name again, that little rascal?

129
00:06:27,950 --> 00:06:29,650
Bon, il est où, du jardin, là ?
So where is he, in the garden?

130
00:06:29,650 --> 00:06:31,690
Il est encore en train de tourner le Déserteur, c'est ça ?
Is he still shooting The Deserter, is that it?

131
00:06:31,690 --> 00:06:32,850
Ils ont encore pris du retard ?
They've fallen behind again?

132
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:34,810
Non, bête, le tournage du Déserteur est bien fini.
No, silly, the shoot for The Deserter is long over.

133
00:06:34,950 --> 00:06:35,430
Y a deux semaines.
Two weeks ago.

134
00:06:35,790 --> 00:06:38,630
Simplement, Jean prend quelques jours de repos avant d'enchaîner avec vous.
Jean's just taking a few days off before joining you.

135
00:06:39,250 --> 00:06:40,130
Il a super hâte.
He's really excited.

136
00:06:40,930 --> 00:06:42,210
Très excité par ce film, tu sais.
Very pumped about this film, you know.

137
00:06:42,350 --> 00:06:43,670
Le tournage commence dans 15 jours.
Shooting starts in 15 days.

138
00:06:43,910 --> 00:06:45,710
Il a des essayages à faire, des répétitions.
He has fittings to do, rehearsals.

139
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:47,150
J'ai 200 personnes qui comptent sur lui, moi.
I've got 200 people counting on him.

140
00:06:47,270 --> 00:06:48,090
12 millions de budget.
12 million budget.

141
00:06:48,270 --> 00:06:50,870
Et ça fait des mois qu'on l'attend à cause de ce Déserteur de merde ?
And we've been waiting months for him because of that god-awful Deserter?

142
00:06:50,870 --> 00:06:53,370
J'ai beaucoup de respect pour le cinéma d'auteur, tu vois ?
I have a lot of respect for arthouse cinema, you know?

143
00:06:53,370 --> 00:06:55,370
Oui, il en faut pour faire plaisir aux professeurs à la retraite.
Yes, well, someone has to keep retired teachers happy.

144
00:06:55,410 --> 00:06:56,110
Je suis d'accord.
Fair enough.

145
00:06:56,850 --> 00:06:59,450
Mais qu'est-ce qu'il est allé faire sur ce tournage interminable
But what was he thinking, signing on to that never-ending shoot

146
00:06:59,450 --> 00:07:00,970
avec cette réalisatrice à moitié folle ?
with that half-mad director?

147
00:07:00,970 --> 00:07:02,830
Solveig Ackerfeld, Grand Prix à Cannes, y a deux ans.
Solveig Ackerfeld, Grand Prix at Cannes two years ago.

148
00:07:02,890 --> 00:07:03,510
Et 50 entrées.
And 50 admissions.

149
00:07:04,150 --> 00:07:05,930
Écoute, on en reparlera quand il aura eu un César.
Look, we'll talk again when she gets a César.

150
00:07:06,030 --> 00:07:06,310
Ah oui.
Ha, right.

151
00:07:06,310 --> 00:07:08,920
Oui. Tiens, regarde. Tu vas voir.
Right. Here, look. You'll see.

152
00:07:10,120 --> 00:07:11,320
C'est des images de tournage.
These are behind-the-scenes shots.

153
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:13,420
C'est archi-confidentiel, mais moi, je suis pas censée les avoir vues.
Strictly confidential — I'm not supposed to have seen them.

154
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:15,020
Mais comme ça, ça va te donner un peu une idée du truc.
But at least it'll give you a bit of an idea.

155
00:07:15,340 --> 00:07:15,880
Tu vas voir.
Watch.

156
00:07:17,100 --> 00:07:17,860
Oh, proche-toi.
Oh, come closer.

157
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:30,040
C'est l'histoire d'un soldat blessé qui a déserté pendant la guerre de 14
It's the story of a wounded soldier who deserted during the Great War

158
00:07:30,520 --> 00:07:32,500
et qui se cache dans la forêt pendant des années
and hides in the forest for years

159
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:33,620
pour échapper à la peine de mort.
to escape the death penalty.

160
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:35,500
On connaît ça.
We know this one.

161
00:08:28,660 --> 00:08:28,980
Coupé.
Cut.

162
00:08:30,710 --> 00:08:31,530
Jean, c'est coupé.
Jean, it's a cut.

163
00:08:34,200 --> 00:08:35,620
Jean, c'est coupé !
Jean, cut!

164
00:08:35,620 --> 00:08:41,280
On peut en refaire une ?
Can we do another take?

165
00:08:41,280 --> 00:08:41,840
Non.
No.

166
00:08:43,860 --> 00:08:44,600
Il est démon.
He's a demon.

167
00:08:45,460 --> 00:08:46,380
T'as vu ça ?
Did you see that?

168
00:08:46,380 --> 00:08:48,560
C'est à la hauteur de DiCaprio dans un revenant.
It's right up there with DiCaprio in The Revenant.

169
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,580
Tu sais que le lapin, là...
You know that rabbit there…

170
00:08:51,430 --> 00:08:52,850
C'est un vrai lapin.
It's a real rabbit.

171
00:08:52,990 --> 00:08:54,410
Bon, ça suffit, les conneries, Andrea.
Alright, enough nonsense, Andrea.

172
00:08:55,310 --> 00:08:56,790
Il est où, du jardin, là ?
So where is he — in the garden?

173
00:09:43,380 --> 00:09:44,900
Il faut que je vous montre.
I have to show you something.

174
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:45,920
Qu'est-ce que c'est ?
What is this?

175
00:09:58,540 --> 00:10:01,890
Oui, on a bossé comme des fous, tu vois.
Yeah, we've been working like crazy, you know.

176
00:10:02,660 --> 00:10:04,720
Mais dire que ça a failli pas se faire...
To think it almost didn't happen…

177
00:10:04,720 --> 00:10:05,840
J'adore l'affiche.
I love the poster.

178
00:10:05,840 --> 00:10:06,560
Elle est trop belle.
It's gorgeous.

179
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:07,540
C'est beau, t'as vu ?
Beautiful, right?

180
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:09,860
C'est pas trop vulgaire, ça va ?
Not too vulgar, is it?

181
00:10:09,860 --> 00:10:11,160
Tu veux un bout de sang ?
You want a drop of blood?

182
00:10:11,160 --> 00:10:11,980
Mais t'es tellement belle.
But you're so beautiful.

183
00:10:12,340 --> 00:10:15,080
Même dans un porno amateur albanais, tu serais pas vulgaire, sauf jaloux.
Even in an Albanian amateur porno, you wouldn't look cheap — jealous, maybe.

184
00:10:17,100 --> 00:10:18,000
Merci, les gars.
Thanks, guys.

185
00:10:18,380 --> 00:10:19,220
Vous me manquez trop.
I miss you all so much.

186
00:10:19,240 --> 00:10:20,020
Mais toi aussi.
We miss you too.

187
00:10:20,140 --> 00:10:22,180
Tu sais que des fois, on va voir Antoine et on lui demande de faire...
You know sometimes we go see Antoine and ask him to do...

188
00:10:24,130 --> 00:10:27,390
Bon, je vais voir mon agent.
Right, I'm off to see my agent.

189
00:10:29,090 --> 00:10:29,330
Merci.
Thank you.

190
00:10:31,810 --> 00:10:33,390
Tu repasses, hein ?
You'll come back, yeah?

191
00:10:37,460 --> 00:10:37,780
Camille ?
Camille?

192
00:10:37,780 --> 00:10:38,920
Camille, où ?
Camille, where?

193
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,760
T'as nul mon rendez-vous de 15h, je vais chez Dujardin.
You cancelled my 3 o'clock, I'm going to Dujardin's.

194
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:42,280
Ça y est ? Tu lui mets ton téléphone ?
Done? You're handing over your phone to him?

195
00:10:42,280 --> 00:10:43,280
Bah non, c'est pour ça que j'y vais.
Well no, that's why I'm going in person.

196
00:10:43,380 --> 00:10:43,980
Oh, putain !
Oh, shit!

197
00:10:43,980 --> 00:10:45,140
Qu'est-ce qui se passe ? Ça va ?
What's going on? You okay?

198
00:10:45,140 --> 00:10:46,500
Ça va, c'est rien.
I'm fine, it's nothing.

199
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:47,620
C'est bon, c'est bon.
It's okay, it's okay.

200
00:10:47,720 --> 00:10:49,520
C'est juste une contraction, ça va.
It's just a contraction, I'm fine.

201
00:10:49,600 --> 00:10:50,180
T'as couché ?
Did you sleep with him?

202
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:50,980
Arrête, t'es con, toi.
Stop it, you're an idiot.

203
00:10:51,800 --> 00:10:52,040
Elle accouche !
She's in labour!

204
00:10:52,040 --> 00:10:53,060
Andrea, couche !
Andrea, down!

205
00:10:53,060 --> 00:10:53,880
Elle accouche !
She's in labour!

206
00:10:53,880 --> 00:10:54,740
Elle accouche !
She's in labour!

207
00:10:54,740 --> 00:10:55,980
T'es vraiment con, toi, par contre ?
Are you actually an idiot?

208
00:10:56,700 --> 00:10:57,200
Ça va ?
You okay?

209
00:10:57,520 --> 00:10:58,040
Ça va ?
You okay?

210
00:10:58,040 --> 00:11:00,000
T'as des contractions rapprochées, là ?
Are the contractions coming close together?

211
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,800
Tu veux pas être reposée pendant ta journée ?
Don't you want to be rested during the day?

212
00:11:01,800 --> 00:11:03,580
Tout le monde se calme, OK ?
Everyone calm down, OK?

213
00:11:03,580 --> 00:11:05,360
C'est pas des contractions de travail, c'est juste que...
These aren't labour contractions, it's just that...

214
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,220
T'es sûre ?
You sure?

215
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:08,920
En fait, non, j'ai un utérus qui est très tonique et qui se contracte souvent.
Actually, no — I have a very toned uterus that contracts frequently.

216
00:11:09,240 --> 00:11:09,980
Voilà, vous savez tout.
Now you know everything.

217
00:11:10,320 --> 00:11:12,160
OK, quand est-ce que tu prends ton congé maternité ?
OK, when are you starting your maternity leave?

218
00:11:12,160 --> 00:11:14,840
Ah, je sais pas, dans une semaine ou deux semaines.
I don't know, in a week or two.

219
00:11:14,920 --> 00:11:15,840
Enfin, quand je le sentirai, quoi.
When I feel the time is right, really.

220
00:11:16,020 --> 00:11:17,280
C'est trop tard, ça, c'est mauvais pour le bébé.
That's too late — that's bad for the baby.

221
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:19,840
Il va être petit, il va être nerveux, il va avoir un cerveau atrophié.
He'll be small, he'll be anxious, he'll have an underdeveloped brain.

222
00:11:20,080 --> 00:11:21,440
Mais ça va, toi, ton fils, à Londres ?
Speaking of which — your son in London doing okay?

223
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,640
Sans cerveau, tu t'en occupes bien ?
Managing fine without a brain, are you?

224
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:24,900
Écoute, Andrea, t'es pas toujours obligée de jouer Wonder Woman, non plus.
Look, Andrea, you don't always have to play Wonder Woman either.

225
00:11:25,140 --> 00:11:27,300
Mais putain, j'aime mon travail, j'ai pas envie de m'arrêter.
God, I love my job, I don't want to stop.

226
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:29,320
Si je m'arrête, je perds un tiers de mon fichier, OK ?
If I stop, I lose a third of my client list, OK?

227
00:11:29,320 --> 00:11:30,200
Ça va, c'est bon, là ?
Alright, we good now?

228
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:31,540
Non, elle est pas parano.
No, she's not paranoid.

229
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:32,900
Les acteurs veulent être nos seuls enfants.
Actors want to be our only babies.

230
00:11:32,980 --> 00:11:34,440
S'ils portent pas la concurrence, elle a raison.
If they can't handle the competition, she's right.

231
00:11:34,660 --> 00:11:35,740
Bon, écoute, tu devrais déléguer.
Look, you should delegate.

232
00:11:35,780 --> 00:11:37,380
On peut très bien prendre en charge une partie de tes clients.
We can easily take on some of your clients.

233
00:11:37,840 --> 00:11:39,680
Attendez, qui a été enceinte, ici ?
Hold on — who here has been pregnant?

234
00:11:39,680 --> 00:11:40,180
Qui ?
Who?

235
00:11:44,580 --> 00:11:46,900
Voilà, personne. Donc personne me dit comment il faut que je sois enceinte.
Right, nobody. So nobody gets to tell me how to be pregnant.

236
00:11:47,630 --> 00:11:47,950
Bouge.
Move.

237
00:11:48,570 --> 00:11:50,390
Tiens, Mathias, tu t'approches pas de mon fichier, t'as compris ?
And Mathias — stay away from my client list, understood?

238
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:07,800
Je sais que c'est pas facile.
I know it's not easy.

239
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:09,920
C'est vrai, on a chacun notre petit tempérament,
True, we each have our own little temperament,

240
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:11,820
et on peut se laisser emporter, c'est humain.
and we can get carried away — it's human.

241
00:12:13,130 --> 00:12:17,680
Mais on avait bien dit qu'on ne parlait pas ici de monde,
But we agreed we weren't talking about that here,

242
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:19,640
et que je gérais ma grossesse à ma femme.
and that I was handling my wife's pregnancy.

243
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:20,740
Bien sûr.
Of course.

244
00:12:21,900 --> 00:12:25,080
C'est juste qu'en tant que patron, je ne fais que me soucier de la santé de mes employés.
It's just that as your boss, I can't help but care about my employees' well-being.

245
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:27,640
Oui, je te remercie de ta bienveillance.
Yes, thank you for your concern.

246
00:12:28,370 --> 00:12:29,970
Mais je reste évidemment à ta disposition
But I'm obviously still available to you

247
00:12:29,970 --> 00:12:32,810
pour toutes les formalités concernant ton congé matrimonial.
for all the formalities regarding your parental leave.

248
00:12:32,830 --> 00:12:33,310
Et ta maternité ?
And your maternity leave?

249
00:12:33,310 --> 00:12:36,330
Je ne manquerai pas de te solliciter, mais c'est vrai que, comme je te l'ai dit,
I'll be sure to reach out, but it's true that, as I told you,

250
00:12:36,430 --> 00:12:38,030
je le ferai lorsque je ressentirai le besoin.
I'll do so when I feel the need.

251
00:12:38,630 --> 00:12:39,290
C'est noté.
Noted.

252
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:42,080
Tout va bien avec ta compagne ?
Everything going well with your partner?

253
00:12:42,080 --> 00:12:43,640
Très bien, merci.
Very well, thank you.

254
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:45,040
J'en suis ravi.
I'm glad to hear it.

255
00:12:45,420 --> 00:12:47,170
Tu lui transmettras mes amitiés.
Do pass along my regards.

256
00:12:47,880 --> 00:12:48,640
J'y manquerai pas.
Will do.

257
00:12:53,110 --> 00:12:53,630
Bonne journée.
Have a good day.

258
00:12:55,500 --> 00:12:55,820
Cordialement.
Best regards.

259
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:02,620
Oui ?
Yes?

260
00:13:04,260 --> 00:13:07,400
Gabriel, un déjeuner avec Norman, demain à 13h, ça te va ?
Gabriel, lunch with Norman tomorrow at 1 PM — does that work for you?

261
00:13:07,400 --> 00:13:08,420
Euh, non.
Uh, no.

262
00:13:09,160 --> 00:13:11,660
Euh, non, demain, ça le fait pas, j'ai beaucoup de trucs.
Uh, no, tomorrow doesn't work, I've got a lot going on.

263
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:13,780
Mais j'ai rien noté, demain, pour le déjeuner.
But I haven't got anything down for lunch tomorrow.

264
00:13:13,780 --> 00:13:15,000
T'as pris un autre rendez-vous ?
Did you make another appointment?

265
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:16,020
Oh, Hervé, ça va, quand même.
Oh, Hervé, come on.

266
00:13:16,120 --> 00:13:18,700
Je sais encore avec qui je déjeune et à quelle heure, non ?
I still know who I'm having lunch with and at what time, don't I?

267
00:13:18,890 --> 00:13:19,270
OK.
OK.

268
00:13:19,610 --> 00:13:22,610
C'est pas comme si t'avais pas parfois des problèmes majeurs d'organisation
It's not as if you don't sometimes have major organizational issues

269
00:13:22,610 --> 00:13:25,850
que seul ton merveilleux assistant avait, André Gézat, qui était capable de résoudre.
that only your wonderful assistant, André Gézat, was able to sort out.

270
00:13:25,930 --> 00:13:27,330
C'est bon ? C'est tout ? Y a autre chose, non ?
Are we done? Is that everything? Nothing else?

271
00:13:27,980 --> 00:13:30,000
Oui, le contrat de Laura Smet a signé vite,
Yes, Laura Smet's contract got signed quickly,

272
00:13:30,080 --> 00:13:32,560
sauf que j'ai l'impression que la jury s'est trompée en le rédigeant,
except I have a feeling the legal team made an error drafting it,

273
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:35,920
parce que, regarde, t'as pas pu négocier ce montant.
because look — there's no way you negotiated that figure.

274
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,460
C'est colossalement faible, non ?
It's colossally low, isn't it?

275
00:13:38,620 --> 00:13:39,860
Il manque pas un chiffre ?
Isn't there a digit missing?

276
00:13:40,360 --> 00:13:43,360
Je te laisse là, je m'en occuperai plus tard. Voilà.
I'll leave you to it — I'll deal with it later. There.

277
00:13:44,520 --> 00:13:45,840
Bon ? Tu me laisses bosser ?
OK? Can you let me get some work done?

278
00:13:45,840 --> 00:14:25,260
Je peux plus rester ici, maman, il nous gâche trop la vie, là !
I can't stay here anymore, Mum — he's ruining our lives!

279
00:14:25,260 --> 00:14:26,690
Tu ne vas nulle part !
You're not going anywhere!

280
00:14:26,690 --> 00:14:29,190
Mais il est complètement taré, c'est un grand malade, ce type !
He's completely unhinged — the guy is seriously messed up!

281
00:14:29,190 --> 00:14:30,410
Tu vas pas comme ça, ton père !
That's your father you're talking about!

282
00:14:30,410 --> 00:14:33,410
C'était mieux quand il faisait son film dans la forêt, au moins, on était tranquilles !
It was better when he was off making his film in the woods — at least we had some peace!

283
00:14:33,410 --> 00:14:34,290
Ça va, Andréa ?
You alright, Andréa?

284
00:14:34,980 --> 00:14:35,780
Ça va, Alice ?
You alright, Alice?

285
00:14:35,780 --> 00:14:36,640
Je viens voir Jean.
I'm here to see Jean.

286
00:14:36,900 --> 00:14:37,940
Il est pas là, je suis désolée.
He's not here, I'm sorry.

287
00:14:38,260 --> 00:14:40,280
Ah bah si ! Justement, il est là, sous les arbres.
Oh, but he is! He's right there, under the trees.

288
00:14:40,560 --> 00:14:41,440
Non, il est pas là !
No, he's not here!

289
00:14:41,440 --> 00:14:42,900
Maman, il est là, arrête de mentir !
Mum, he's there — stop lying!

290
00:14:42,900 --> 00:14:44,460
Je te jure qu'elle peut nous aider, elle !
I swear she can help us!

291
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:48,360
Il a confisqué tous nos écrans, il veut plus qu'on allume les lumières !
He's confiscated all our screens — he won't let us turn the lights on!

292
00:14:48,360 --> 00:14:51,060
Eh mais sauvez-nous, s'il vous plaît, pitié, sauvez-nous, là, parce que...
Please, save us — please, please save us, because…

293
00:15:13,590 --> 00:15:14,150
Jean ?
Jean?

294
00:15:15,060 --> 00:15:15,620
Hein ?
Hmm?

295
00:15:17,130 --> 00:15:18,350
Eh, Andréa !
Hey, Andréa!

296
00:15:21,710 --> 00:15:23,370
Fallait pas te déplacer, je suis passé à l'agence.
You didn't have to come all the way out here — I stopped by the agency.

297
00:15:26,650 --> 00:15:29,330
Putain, il y a urgence, là, douche, pressing, euh...
God, it's urgent — shower, dry-cleaning, uh…

298
00:15:29,910 --> 00:15:31,630
Ouais, c'est ce que me dit ma femme, aussi, ouais.
Yeah, my wife says the same thing, yeah.

299
00:15:32,190 --> 00:15:33,270
T'inquiète pas, c'est pas grave.
Don't worry, it's fine.

300
00:15:33,430 --> 00:15:35,570
C'est l'odeur de la terre, j'assure.
It's the smell of the earth — trust me.

301
00:15:35,730 --> 00:15:36,490
De la putréfaction.
Putrefaction.

302
00:15:37,070 --> 00:15:38,990
Vous vivez dans un monde qui est tellement aseptisé, aussi.
You live in such a sanitized world too.

303
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:45,780
Ça, c'est une buse, ça.
That there's a buzzard.

304
00:15:48,570 --> 00:15:50,370
Tu vois, elle tourne autour.
See, it's circling.

305
00:15:51,230 --> 00:15:52,330
Elle vient me chourer, mais là, pas.
It's coming to steal from me, but not today.

306
00:16:00,510 --> 00:16:00,790
Bon.
Right.

307
00:16:01,370 --> 00:16:01,870
Jean ?
Jean?

308
00:16:02,460 --> 00:16:03,040
Hein ?
Hm?

309
00:16:03,040 --> 00:16:03,300
Ouais.
Yeah.

310
00:16:03,910 --> 00:16:04,690
Je pense que...
I think that...

311
00:16:10,680 --> 00:16:11,220
Jean ?
Jean?

312
00:16:11,220 --> 00:16:12,060
Oui ?
Yes?

313
00:16:12,060 --> 00:16:15,520
Écoute, visiblement, t'es très marqué par ton rôle dans le Déserteur,
Look, clearly, you're very marked by your role in The Deserter,

314
00:16:15,580 --> 00:16:18,660
et c'est normal, parce que c'est un rôle, c'est très physique, c'est très fort.
and that's understandable, because it's a very physical role, very intense.

315
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:20,320
J'ai jamais vécu ça avant, ouais, jamais.
I've never experienced anything like it before. Never.

316
00:16:20,480 --> 00:16:23,100
Ouais, je sais, mais là, ils t'attendent pour le tournage.
Yeah, I know, but they're waiting for you on set.

317
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:25,020
Tu sais, le film où tu dois jouer un banquier ?
You know, the film where you play a banker?

318
00:16:25,020 --> 00:16:26,100
Je sais, je sais, Andréa, mais...
I know, I know, Andréa, but...

319
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:28,420
Franchement, là, je peux pas, quoi.
Honestly, I just can't right now.

320
00:16:29,770 --> 00:16:31,190
Je peux pas enchaîner comme ça.
I can't jump straight into something else like this.

321
00:16:32,520 --> 00:16:33,340
Tu comprends ?
Do you understand?

322
00:16:35,060 --> 00:16:37,600
J'ai passé six mois dans la forêt, je me suis dépouillé de tout.
I spent six months in the forest, I stripped everything away.

323
00:16:38,400 --> 00:16:39,520
Ça m'a fait un bien, mais...
It did me a world of good, but...

324
00:16:41,950 --> 00:16:45,730
Je suis allé à l'os, à l'os de l'humain, tu comprends ?
I got down to the bone — the bare human bone. You understand?

325
00:16:47,650 --> 00:16:50,900
Alors, l'idée de me retrouver, là, dans une tour,
So the idea of ending up in some tower,

326
00:16:51,220 --> 00:16:53,620
dans la Défense, avec le bruit, les gens, la lumière...
in La Défense, with the noise, the people, the lights...

327
00:16:57,780 --> 00:16:58,780
On peut pas temporiser ?
Can't we stall for time?

328
00:16:58,780 --> 00:16:59,880
Ben, Jean, non, on peut pas, là.
Jean, no, we really can't.

329
00:17:00,340 --> 00:17:02,100
Enfin, tu vois, on les a déjà beaucoup fait attendre.
I mean, we've already kept them waiting a long time.

330
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:04,340
Non, mais t'as même pas signé ton contrat, en plus.
And you haven't even signed your contract yet, on top of everything.

331
00:17:04,580 --> 00:17:05,400
Si, je l'ai signé, hein.
I did sign it, actually.

332
00:17:05,680 --> 00:17:06,720
T'as signé Émile Berthier.
You signed it as Émile Berthier.

333
00:17:08,430 --> 00:17:08,810
Ah, oui.
Oh. Right.

334
00:17:11,420 --> 00:17:12,600
C'est ton personnage, Jean.
That's your character, Jean.

335
00:17:12,800 --> 00:17:13,480
C'est pas toi.
That's not you.

336
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:14,340
Oui, je sais, oui.
Yes, I know. Yes.

337
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:17,940
Tu veux que je t'aide à dégager les...
Do you want me to help you clear the...

338
00:17:18,340 --> 00:17:19,060
Non, non, c'est bon.
No, no, it's fine.

339
00:17:20,730 --> 00:17:20,970
OK.
OK.

340
00:17:21,590 --> 00:17:22,310
Mais tu sais, déjà,
But you know, for starters,

341
00:17:22,550 --> 00:17:23,930
si t'enlèves ton costume, ça va aller beaucoup mieux.
if you take off that costume, you'll feel a lot better.

342
00:17:24,170 --> 00:17:24,610
Ouais ?
Yeah?

343
00:17:24,610 --> 00:17:26,750
Ouais. Puis là, ce soir, tu te fais couler un bon bain chaud,
Yeah. And tonight, run yourself a nice hot bath,

344
00:17:26,930 --> 00:17:29,110
tu te fais un bon gommage, tu frottes, tu frottes fort,
give yourself a good scrub — really scrub, scrub hard,

345
00:17:29,270 --> 00:17:30,850
tu prends le côté vert de l'éponge.
use the rough side of the sponge.

346
00:17:31,470 --> 00:17:33,150
Et je peux pas le garder ?
And I can't keep it?

347
00:17:33,150 --> 00:17:33,890
Quoi donc ?
Keep what?

348
00:17:33,890 --> 00:17:34,410
Le manteau.
The coat.

349
00:17:35,140 --> 00:17:35,700
Pour ?
For?

350
00:17:36,140 --> 00:17:36,420
Pour...
For...

351
00:17:37,830 --> 00:17:38,650
Pour le banquier ?
For the banker?

352
00:17:38,650 --> 00:17:38,990
Oui.
Yes.

353
00:17:41,030 --> 00:17:43,210
Ça ferait un banquier un peu atypique, mais c'est intéressant, aussi.
It'd make for a rather unconventional banker, but it's interesting, I'll give you that.

354
00:17:43,250 --> 00:17:44,390
Non, Jean, vraiment, je te jure,
No, Jean, I'm serious, I swear,

355
00:17:44,450 --> 00:17:46,330
je pense que je préfère bouffer la cervelle du lapin mort
I'd rather eat the brains out of that dead rabbit

356
00:17:46,330 --> 00:17:47,810
que de valider ce manteau dans ton contrat.
than approve that coat in your contract.

357
00:17:51,510 --> 00:17:53,810
Moi, je crois que très tôt, on a déjà en soi qui on va devenir.
I believe that very early on, we already carry inside us who we're going to become.

358
00:17:56,240 --> 00:17:57,380
Tu vois, la voie qu'on choisit,
The path we choose —

359
00:17:57,840 --> 00:17:59,960
si on y réfléchit bien, elle est déjà là depuis l'enfance.
if you think about it carefully, it's already there from childhood.

360
00:18:01,520 --> 00:18:02,320
Toi, par exemple,
You, for example,

361
00:18:02,760 --> 00:18:04,660
quel est le truc que t'adorais faire quand t'étais gamin ?
What was the thing you loved doing as a kid?

362
00:18:05,280 --> 00:18:07,720
Le truc que tu faisais quand t'étais seul qui te distinguait des autres.
The thing you did when you were alone that set you apart from everyone else.

363
00:18:09,740 --> 00:18:11,280
Je sais pas, j'y ai jamais réfléchi.
I don't know, I've never really thought about it.

364
00:18:11,860 --> 00:18:13,400
Tu sais, j'ai un pote architecte,
You know, I have a friend who's an architect,

365
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:16,910
quand il était gamin, il passait sa vie à construire des cabanes.
and when he was a kid, he spent his whole life building forts.

366
00:18:17,590 --> 00:18:19,190
Il faisait que ça, cabane, cabane, cabane.
That's all he did — fort, fort, fort.

367
00:18:20,950 --> 00:18:21,270
Allez...
Come on...

368
00:18:21,270 --> 00:18:23,490
Eh, t'avais forcément un truc, hein ?
Hey, you had to have something, right?

369
00:18:24,010 --> 00:18:26,030
C'est vrai, c'est drôle.
True, that's funny.

370
00:18:27,460 --> 00:18:29,040
Moi, c'était les jeux de stratégie.
For me, it was strategy games.

371
00:18:29,770 --> 00:18:30,650
Les échecs, surtout.
Chess, mostly.

372
00:18:31,170 --> 00:18:32,030
Le bas-gamin, aussi.
Backgammon, too.

373
00:18:33,270 --> 00:18:35,730
J'y jouais énormément, tout seul.
I played it constantly, on my own.

374
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:38,680
Je me dédoublais, je faisais les deux joueurs à la fois.
I'd split myself in two, play both sides at once.

375
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:39,360
Voilà.
There you go.

376
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:41,740
Et t'es devenu agent, c'est pas beau, ça ?
And you became an agent — pretty fitting, no?

377
00:18:41,740 --> 00:18:47,170
Et toi, alors ? C'était quoi ?
What about you, then? What was it?

378
00:18:47,680 --> 00:18:48,380
Commander.
Giving orders.

379
00:18:50,300 --> 00:18:50,660
Ouais.
Yeah.

380
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:53,880
Quand on jouait au foot, c'était pas être dans l'équipe, moi, ce que je voulais.
When we played football, it wasn't about being on the team for me.

381
00:18:55,070 --> 00:18:56,350
C'était diriger l'équipe.
It was about running the team.

382
00:18:58,080 --> 00:19:00,060
C'est marrant, hein ?
Funny, right?

383
00:19:04,780 --> 00:19:05,760
20h30, sharp !
8:30, sharp!

384
00:19:05,760 --> 00:19:06,840
C'est comme je les aime.
Just how I like it.

385
00:19:09,200 --> 00:19:10,520
Ça va, les Wonder Boys ?
All good, Wonder Boys?

386
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:11,100
Ça va, champion ?
How you doing, champ?

387
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:13,560
Salut.
Hey.

388
00:19:13,600 --> 00:19:14,080
Comment tu vas ?
How are you?

389
00:19:14,080 --> 00:19:14,740
Super.
Great.

390
00:19:15,060 --> 00:19:15,360
Bonsoir.
Good evening.

391
00:19:15,600 --> 00:19:16,940
Je vous présente Mathias Barneville.
Let me introduce Mathias Barneville.

392
00:19:18,790 --> 00:19:22,250
Avec moi, chez ASK, Nico, Jérémy.
With me at ASK — Nico, Jérémy.

393
00:19:22,950 --> 00:19:23,630
C'est mes amis.
These are my friends.

394
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:25,580
Bon, parfois, mes partenaires.
Well, sometimes my partners.

395
00:19:27,030 --> 00:19:32,280
Je leur ai parlé d'ASK et de mon envie de développer des nouvelles branches, tu sais.
I told them about ASK and my idea to develop new branches, you know.

396
00:19:33,170 --> 00:19:34,890
Comme je l'ai fait avec la gestion des droits publicitaires.
Like I did with the advertising rights management.

397
00:19:35,550 --> 00:19:37,170
Ils vont m'aider à dépoussiérer un peu tout ça.
They're going to help me shake things up a bit.

398
00:19:38,540 --> 00:19:39,300
T'en veux ?
Want some?

399
00:19:41,980 --> 00:19:42,300
Allez.
Go on.

400
00:19:42,680 --> 00:19:43,420
OK, les gars ?
We good, guys?

401
00:19:43,960 --> 00:19:44,560
À la tienne.
Cheers.

402
00:19:44,640 --> 00:19:45,200
À la tienne.
Cheers.

403
00:19:45,320 --> 00:19:45,820
Allez, santé.
Come on, cheers.

404
00:19:50,180 --> 00:19:51,740
Non, mais je t'assure, c'était un vrai traquenard.
No, I'm telling you, it was a complete setup.

405
00:19:52,580 --> 00:19:56,500
Moi, je pensais qu'on allait se retrouver avec Hicham pour discuter de l'avenir de l'agence.
I thought it was just going to be me and Hicham talking about the agency's future.

406
00:19:57,140 --> 00:19:59,620
Et puis, il y a ces deux types qui arrivent avec leur tête arrogante, là,
And then these two guys show up with their smug faces,

407
00:19:59,620 --> 00:20:02,160
avec lesquels il veut s'associer et développer des nouvelles branches.
and he wants to partner with them and develop new branches.

408
00:20:02,940 --> 00:20:03,580
Complètement ubuesques.
Completely absurd.

409
00:20:04,390 --> 00:20:06,630
Chéri, c'est son argent. Laisse le faire.
Honey, it's his money. Let him do what he wants.

410
00:20:07,630 --> 00:20:08,790
Oui, mais ça concerne ASK.
Yes, but this involves ASK.

411
00:20:09,530 --> 00:20:10,190
Adresse ton dos.
Straighten your back.

412
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:15,900
À un moment, il y a même un des deux types qui a proposé qu'on fasse du conseil en images
At one point, one of the two guys even suggested we do image consulting

413
00:20:15,900 --> 00:20:17,500
pour les sportifs et les hommes politiques.
for athletes and politicians.

414
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:19,940
Et Hicham qui dit pas oui, pourquoi pas ?
And Hicham says, not no — why not?

415
00:20:19,940 --> 00:20:21,240
Non, mais où on va, là ?
No, but where are we headed here?

416
00:20:22,620 --> 00:20:25,280
Tu sais, la bonne nouvelle, c'est que c'est un polémique, ce garçon,
You know, the good news is he's someone who stirs things up,

417
00:20:26,180 --> 00:20:27,520
et qu'il va vouloir tout faire en même temps.
and he's going to want to do everything at once.

418
00:20:28,450 --> 00:20:31,010
Et forcément, il sera beaucoup moins présent chez ASK.
Which means he'll naturally be much less present at ASK.

419
00:20:32,210 --> 00:20:36,530
Et si la boîte marche bien, il va pas tarder à vous laisser gérer comme vous le voulez.
And if the company does well, it won't be long before he lets you run it the way you want.

420
00:20:39,820 --> 00:20:41,040
Il faudrait qu'il nomme un DG.
He'd need to appoint a Managing Director.

421
00:20:41,480 --> 00:20:52,770
Un nouvel homme fort. ASK qui connaît bien la boîte.
A new strongman. Someone who knows the company well.

422
00:20:52,850 --> 00:20:56,700
Il fait du yoga avec sa femme pour lui faire plaisir.
He does yoga with his wife to make her happy.

423
00:20:57,970 --> 00:21:01,230
Ça me déplie pas, tu sais. Ça me détend, même.
It doesn't bother me, you know. It actually relaxes me.

424
00:21:03,060 --> 00:21:03,760
C'est vrai ?
Really?

425
00:21:03,760 --> 00:21:11,980
C'est important qu'on fasse des choses tous les deux, tu sais.
It's important we do things together, you know.

426
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:17,140
Babette Solis me harcèle. Elle a toujours pas reçu le contrat de jambes.
Babette Solis is hounding me. She still hasn't received the leg contract.

427
00:21:17,980 --> 00:21:19,100
Rappelle-la, temporise.
Call her back, stall.

428
00:21:20,490 --> 00:21:21,310
Mais comment ?
But how?

429
00:21:21,310 --> 00:21:22,170
Tu me rends à deux.
You're making me crazy.

430
00:21:24,270 --> 00:21:26,010
Tu dis que t'as envoyé le contrat à la mauvaise adresse.
Tell her you sent the contract to the wrong address.

431
00:21:26,150 --> 00:21:26,950
Tu te démerdes pas.
You're useless.

432
00:21:26,950 --> 00:21:27,830
On va passer pour une conne.
We're going to look like idiots.

433
00:21:27,830 --> 00:21:29,250
C'est à ça que ça sert, les assistants.
That's what assistants are for.

434
00:21:29,510 --> 00:21:31,910
Je suis agent, maman. Faut que je fasse un peu gaffe à ma crédibilité.
I'm an agent, Mom. I need to watch my credibility a little.

435
00:21:32,070 --> 00:21:33,290
T'inquiète, personne te connaît.
Don't worry, nobody knows you.

436
00:21:33,510 --> 00:21:34,190
Salut, tout le monde.
Hey, everyone.

437
00:21:35,260 --> 00:21:35,580
Bonjour.
Hello.

438
00:21:35,860 --> 00:21:36,480
Bonjour, Noémie.
Hello, Noémie.

439
00:21:36,700 --> 00:21:36,800
Bonjour.
Hello.

440
00:21:38,720 --> 00:21:45,360
On a quoi à l'ordre du jour ?
What's on the agenda?

441
00:21:46,100 --> 00:21:46,860
Genre du jardin.
Garden variety stuff.

442
00:21:51,990 --> 00:21:54,250
Le tournage est fini depuis deux semaines et il est toujours comme ça.
Filming wrapped two weeks ago and he's still like this.

443
00:21:55,160 --> 00:21:56,400
Et il doit enchaîner avec l'autre film.
And he's supposed to go straight into the next film.

444
00:21:57,700 --> 00:21:59,350
C'est un cauchemar, les gars.
It's a nightmare, guys.

445
00:21:59,830 --> 00:22:01,470
Mais il veut pas se laver ou se raser ?
But he won't wash or shave?

446
00:22:02,690 --> 00:22:03,190
Rien ?
Nothing?

447
00:22:03,190 --> 00:22:04,350
Non, rien. Rien.
No, nothing. Nothing.

448
00:22:05,500 --> 00:22:06,920
À ce propos, Gabrielle me demandait,
On that note, Gabrielle was asking —

449
00:22:06,960 --> 00:22:08,700
ton nouveau style, c'est pour faire brancher
is the new look something you're going for

450
00:22:08,700 --> 00:22:10,700
ou t'as juste lâché l'affaire physiquement ?
or have you just let yourself go?

451
00:22:10,730 --> 00:22:12,830
Arlette, c'est pas parce que t'es vieille que tu peux tout te permettre.
Arlette, just because you're old doesn't mean you can say whatever you want.

452
00:22:13,720 --> 00:22:15,840
Non, mais parfois, y a des mystères qui ressemblent à des clochards.
No, but sometimes there are mysteries that look like bums.

453
00:22:16,420 --> 00:22:17,240
On s'y perd, hein.
You lose track, don't you.

454
00:22:18,140 --> 00:22:19,140
Et puis, vieille, t'es marrante.
And old — you're a funny one.

455
00:22:19,940 --> 00:22:22,280
Faut encore y arriver. Y en a plein qui meurent avant.
You've still got to make it there. Plenty of people die before.

456
00:22:22,540 --> 00:22:23,500
OK, les gars, pardon.
OK, guys, sorry.

457
00:22:24,100 --> 00:22:25,240
On peut rester focus, là ?
Can we stay focused here?

458
00:22:25,240 --> 00:22:26,660
Parce que moi, j'ai un acteur en pleine Delewis.
Because I've got an actor in full-on Delewis mode.

459
00:22:27,060 --> 00:22:28,060
En pleine quoi ?
Full-on what?

460
00:22:28,060 --> 00:22:28,920
Daniel Delewis.
Daniel Delewis.

461
00:22:29,670 --> 00:22:31,310
L'acteur anglais qui travaille tellement ses rôles
The English actor who gets so deep into his roles

462
00:22:31,310 --> 00:22:32,130
qu'après, il peut plus en sortir.
he can't come back out afterwards.

463
00:22:32,950 --> 00:22:35,110
Ça peut servir la culture cinématographique
A little film culture can come in handy

464
00:22:35,110 --> 00:22:36,810
quand on dirige une agence artistique.
when you run a talent agency.

465
00:22:37,550 --> 00:22:39,210
Par exemple, pour Le Dernier des Mohicans,
For instance, for The Last of the Mohicans,

466
00:22:39,930 --> 00:22:42,010
Daniel Delewis a vécu comme un Indien pendant six mois.
Daniel Delewis lived like a Native American for six months.

467
00:22:42,090 --> 00:22:42,890
Et quand ça s'est terminé,
And when it was over,

468
00:22:42,910 --> 00:22:44,650
il voulait toujours dormir avec son fusil à poudre.
he still wanted to sleep with his flintlock rifle.

469
00:22:45,010 --> 00:22:46,150
Et après Miley Foot,
And after My Left Foot,

470
00:22:46,210 --> 00:22:47,890
il a continué à écrire des lettres avec ses pieds.
he kept writing letters with his feet.

471
00:22:48,310 --> 00:22:49,230
Méthode acteur studio.
Method acting.

472
00:22:49,570 --> 00:22:49,990
Ah ouais ?
Oh yeah?

473
00:22:50,370 --> 00:22:52,070
Santé mentale fragile, le garçon ?
Fragile mental state, that man?

474
00:22:52,070 --> 00:22:53,350
Moi, je trouve ça magnifique.
I think it's beautiful.

475
00:22:53,370 --> 00:22:55,630
C'est une chance d'être tellement bouleversé en profondeur
It's a gift to be shaken that deeply —

476
00:22:55,630 --> 00:22:57,050
parce que tu fais que t'es transformé.
because what you do transforms you.

477
00:22:57,070 --> 00:22:57,790
Tu deviens un autre.
You become someone else.

478
00:22:58,230 --> 00:22:59,390
Bon, mais j'ai pas bien compris.
Right, but I didn't quite follow.

479
00:22:59,690 --> 00:23:01,250
Finalement, il a signé son contrat
In the end, did he sign his contract

480
00:23:01,470 --> 00:23:01,930
et il l'a pas signé.
or didn't he?

481
00:23:02,670 --> 00:23:04,190
Oui, enfin, non, c'est en cours.
Yeah, well, no, it's in progress.

482
00:23:04,390 --> 00:23:04,750
Parce que...
Because...

483
00:23:05,590 --> 00:23:07,270
Attends, tu vas pas commencer à frétiller, toi, là.
Hold on, don't start getting all excited now.

484
00:23:07,370 --> 00:23:07,610
C'est pas...
It's not...

485
00:23:08,430 --> 00:23:10,310
Peut-être que s'il est possédé,
Maybe if he's possessed,

486
00:23:10,330 --> 00:23:12,550
il faut tout simplement commencer par le désembouter.
we just need to start by unblocking him.

487
00:23:12,950 --> 00:23:16,520
Je connais un très bon chaman à épiner sur scène.
I know a great shaman who can pin him down on stage.

488
00:23:16,800 --> 00:23:17,300
Noémie, tu sais,
Noémie, you know,

489
00:23:17,400 --> 00:23:19,140
je préférerais vraiment une solution dans le monde réel,
I'd really prefer a solution in the real world,

490
00:23:19,160 --> 00:23:19,940
si ça t'embête pas.
if you don't mind.

491
00:23:21,160 --> 00:23:21,940
Chacun sa réalité.
To each their own reality.

492
00:23:22,820 --> 00:23:24,060
Bon, alors il fait quoi, Daniel Delewis,
So what does Daniel Delewis do

493
00:23:24,120 --> 00:23:25,580
pour sortir de ses rôles ?
to get out of his roles?

494
00:23:25,900 --> 00:23:27,140
Vas-y, Mathias, apprends-moi des choses.
Go on, Mathias, teach me something.

495
00:23:27,660 --> 00:23:28,300
Des chaussures.
Shoes.

496
00:23:28,970 --> 00:23:29,610
En Italie.
In Italy.

497
00:23:29,630 --> 00:23:30,310
Avec un bottier.
With a cobbler.

498
00:23:30,690 --> 00:23:32,230
Ça l'aide à se retrouver lui-même.
It helps him find himself again.

499
00:23:32,330 --> 00:23:32,770
Oui.
Yes.

500
00:23:33,230 --> 00:23:34,810
Sinon, dans le genre rapide de par Dieu raconte
Otherwise, along the lines of a quick — God, get this —

501
00:23:34,810 --> 00:23:36,210
que pour sortir du personnage de Rodin,
to get out of the character of Rodin,

502
00:23:36,290 --> 00:23:37,210
il s'est pris une énorme cuillite.
he went on a massive bender.

503
00:23:37,430 --> 00:23:38,230
Ah bon ?
Really?

504
00:23:58,390 --> 00:23:59,550
Vous avez soif, les filles ?
Are you girls thirsty?

505
00:23:59,550 --> 00:24:01,330
Attends, à la fin du Déserteur, ça se fête.
Wait, the end of The Deserter calls for a celebration.

506
00:24:01,690 --> 00:24:02,430
Tu m'étonnes.
You're telling me.

507
00:24:03,150 --> 00:24:04,410
C'est le Grand Cru.
This is the Grand Cru.

508
00:24:05,270 --> 00:24:06,370
Ton préféré, mon amour.
Your favourite, my love.

509
00:24:06,930 --> 00:24:08,370
T'as vu comme c'est revenu, là ?
See how it came back just now?

510
00:24:08,370 --> 00:24:08,570
Ouais.
Yeah.

511
00:24:08,830 --> 00:24:09,590
T'as vu, regarde, je peux faire ça.
See, look, I can do this.

512
00:24:11,610 --> 00:24:11,930
Bien.
Good.

513
00:24:12,750 --> 00:24:13,590
Tu sais quoi ?
You know what?

514
00:24:15,430 --> 00:24:16,830
Encore une petite léchette pour les mains.
One more little splash for the hands.

515
00:24:17,890 --> 00:24:19,130
Pour les mains, pour les mains.
For the hands, for the hands.

516
00:24:23,140 --> 00:24:25,860
À toi, à la fin du Déserteur
To you, to the end of The Deserter

517
00:24:25,860 --> 00:24:26,760
et à ton prochain film.
and to your next film.

518
00:24:30,930 --> 00:24:31,250
Culsac.
Culsac.

519
00:24:40,190 --> 00:24:41,310
Je trinque, mais je bois pas.
I'll toast, but I won't drink.

520
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:44,160
Akerfeld a été très clair, pas d'alcool.
Akerfeld was very clear — no alcohol.

521
00:24:45,460 --> 00:24:48,480
Et ça m'a réussi plutôt pas mal, non ?
And it's worked out pretty well for me, hasn't it?

522
00:24:48,480 --> 00:25:00,540
Il y a une buse, là.
There's a buzzard over there.

523
00:25:01,670 --> 00:25:03,410
C'est la famille des buses, mais...
It's in the buzzard family, but...

524
00:25:03,410 --> 00:25:04,150
Bon, j'appelle Akerfeld.
Right, I'm calling Akerfeld.

525
00:25:04,430 --> 00:25:06,010
...un buzillon ou un truc comme ça.
...a little buzzard or something like that.

526
00:25:06,590 --> 00:25:08,210
Solveig, tu me vois ?
Solveig, can you see me?

527
00:25:08,610 --> 00:25:08,990
Jean.
Jean.

528
00:25:09,190 --> 00:25:09,790
Tu m'entends ?
Can you hear me?

529
00:25:09,790 --> 00:25:10,670
Jean, je t'entends.
Jean, I can hear you.

530
00:25:10,870 --> 00:25:12,530
Je te vois. Tu me vois ou pas ?
I can see you. Can you see me or not?

531
00:25:12,530 --> 00:25:14,030
Je t'entends, je te vois.
I can hear you, I can see you.

532
00:25:15,230 --> 00:25:15,610
Regarde.
Look.

533
00:25:16,030 --> 00:25:16,730
Ça fait...
It's been...

534
00:25:17,780 --> 00:25:18,780
Je l'ai gardé.
I kept it.

535
00:25:19,360 --> 00:25:19,960
Ah oui.
Oh yes.

536
00:25:20,200 --> 00:25:20,860
C'est le vrai, hein ?
It's the real one, right?

537
00:25:20,860 --> 00:25:22,820
Ah oui, Jean, je vois.
Oh yes, Jean, I can see.

538
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:25,780
C'était un tournage...
That was a shoot...

539
00:25:25,780 --> 00:25:27,120
C'était fou, hein ?
It was incredible, wasn't it?

540
00:25:27,120 --> 00:25:27,180
...très fort.
...very powerful.

541
00:25:27,580 --> 00:25:30,840
Nous avons traversé des choses ensemble,
We've been through things together,

542
00:25:31,100 --> 00:25:32,980
des choses, des grandes choses.
things, big things.

543
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:36,740
Et grâce à toi, on a...
And thanks to you, we've...

544
00:25:37,300 --> 00:25:38,780
Non, c'est toi qui m'as donné...
No, it's you who gave me...

545
00:25:38,780 --> 00:25:42,050
Jean, grâce à ton travail,
Jean, thanks to your work,

546
00:25:42,190 --> 00:25:44,010
mais c'était un travail, Jean.
but it was a job, Jean.

547
00:25:44,190 --> 00:25:44,690
Oui.
Yes.

548
00:25:44,810 --> 00:25:49,610
Un travail avec un début, un milieu et une fin.
A job with a beginning, a middle, and an end.

549
00:25:50,500 --> 00:25:51,520
Tu comprends ?
You understand?

550
00:25:51,520 --> 00:25:52,220
Oui.
Yes.

551
00:25:52,220 --> 00:25:54,280
Et aujourd'hui, c'est fini.
And today, it's over.

552
00:25:56,050 --> 00:25:58,430
Tu peux vivre ta vie maintenant avec...
You can live your life now with...

553
00:25:59,110 --> 00:26:01,750
Avec ta famille, ton whisky, ton...
With your family, your whisky, your...

554
00:26:02,210 --> 00:26:03,450
Tout ce que tu veux.
Whatever you want.

555
00:26:03,750 --> 00:26:04,910
Oui, mais je...
Yes, but I...

556
00:26:05,530 --> 00:26:07,110
Solveig, je voulais te parler d'un truc, en fait.
Solveig, I actually wanted to talk to you about something.

557
00:26:07,230 --> 00:26:08,730
J'imaginais, on aurait pu aussi faire
I was thinking, we could also do

558
00:26:08,730 --> 00:26:10,270
le Déserteur 2.
The Deserter 2.

559
00:26:10,750 --> 00:26:11,870
Ça permettait, en fait...
It would allow us to, actually...

560
00:26:11,870 --> 00:26:12,070
Non.
No.

561
00:26:14,120 --> 00:26:16,020
Il n'y a qu'un seul Déserteur.
There's only one Deserter.

562
00:26:16,940 --> 00:26:17,760
Et il est fini.
And it's done.

563
00:26:18,180 --> 00:26:18,940
C'est coupé.
It's a wrap.

564
00:26:18,980 --> 00:26:20,320
Jean, tu comprends ça ?
Jean, do you understand that?

565
00:26:20,320 --> 00:26:21,720
Oui, mais ça permettrait d'en...
Yes, but it would let us...

566
00:26:21,720 --> 00:26:23,380
Non, mais passe à autre chose.
No, move on.

567
00:26:23,580 --> 00:26:25,460
Fais des films, d'autres films.
Make films, other films.

568
00:26:25,800 --> 00:26:25,960
Oui.
Yes.

569
00:26:26,340 --> 00:26:28,240
Je vais en faire, mais ça permettrait de faire...
I will, but it would let us do...

570
00:26:28,240 --> 00:26:30,360
Dans le Déserteur 2, on pourrait avoir plus de forêts,
In The Deserter 2, we could have more forests,

571
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:34,580
plus de bêtes sauvages, plus de mutilations.
more wild animals, more mutilations.

572
00:26:38,490 --> 00:26:38,730
Jean.
Jean.

573
00:27:14,540 --> 00:27:16,160
Fais doucement, quand même, parce que c'est...
Take it easy though, because it's...

574
00:27:26,780 --> 00:27:27,020
Allez.
Come on.

575
00:27:35,340 --> 00:27:51,720
Je peux te laisser finir ?
Can I let you finish?

576
00:27:53,660 --> 00:27:55,180
Non, mais c'est normal que ça prenne un peu de temps.
No, it's normal that it takes a little time.

577
00:27:55,280 --> 00:27:56,800
Tout le monde se précipite pas encore dans mon bureau.
People aren't exactly rushing to my office yet.

578
00:27:58,060 --> 00:27:59,300
Peut-être parce que j'ai pas de bureau.
Maybe because I don't have an office.

579
00:27:59,480 --> 00:28:01,480
Mais je sais bien que ça tombe pas tout qui dans le bec.
But I know things don't just fall into your lap.

580
00:28:01,620 --> 00:28:03,160
Mais enfin, ce qui m'énerve, c'est que toi,
But what gets me is that you,

581
00:28:03,220 --> 00:28:05,220
tu es quelqu'un de bien dans ce milieu de fauves, là.
you're a decent person in this jungle.

582
00:28:05,380 --> 00:28:06,820
Ils le voient pas, ça, les acteurs ?
Don't the actors see that?

583
00:28:08,220 --> 00:28:09,160
Qu'est-ce que tu manges ?
What are you eating?

584
00:28:09,880 --> 00:28:10,540
Une taboulette quinoa.
A quinoa tabbouleh.

585
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:12,780
Ah, ben voilà, ça y est, ils t'ont contaminée.
Ah, there it is, they've got to you.

586
00:28:13,320 --> 00:28:14,720
Alors, déjà, ils t'ont coupé les cheveux,
First they cut your hair,

587
00:28:15,060 --> 00:28:16,220
après, ils te font travailler la nuit,
then they have you working nights,

588
00:28:16,260 --> 00:28:18,800
maintenant, ils vont t'affamer une salade de quinoa.
now they're going to starve you with a quinoa salad.

589
00:28:19,460 --> 00:28:20,440
Allez, va te coucher, va.
Go get some sleep, go on.

590
00:28:20,600 --> 00:28:21,700
Tu me fais de la peine, là.
You're breaking my heart.

591
00:28:21,780 --> 00:28:23,200
On dirait un petit haricot blanc tout sec.
You look like a shriveled little white bean.

592
00:28:23,440 --> 00:28:24,700
Non, je peux pas aller me coucher, là.
No, I can't go to sleep right now.

593
00:28:24,760 --> 00:28:25,780
J'ai encore deux scénarios à lire.
I've still got two scripts to read.

594
00:28:26,460 --> 00:28:28,240
Mais t'inquiète pas, je fais des micro-siestes dans la journée.
Don't worry though, I take micro-naps during the day.

595
00:28:28,300 --> 00:28:29,140
Je vais me planquer dans les toilettes.
I sneak off to the bathroom.

596
00:28:29,740 --> 00:28:30,180
Personne me voit.
Nobody sees me.

597
00:28:30,220 --> 00:28:31,780
10 minutes, ça me suffit pour me reposer, après, ça va mieux.
10 minutes is enough to rest, after that I'm fine.

598
00:28:31,780 --> 00:28:33,460
Non, mais c'est affolant, quand même.
No, but it's alarming, honestly.

599
00:28:34,200 --> 00:28:36,000
C'est pas possible, c'est un monde où on est content
It's not right, this is a world where people are happy

600
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,760
d'aller dormir 10 minutes par terre dans les toilettes.
to sleep 10 minutes on a bathroom floor.

601
00:28:38,380 --> 00:28:40,140
Il faut retrouver une dignité, ma fille, là.
You need to find some dignity, sweetheart. Come on.

602
00:28:40,600 --> 00:28:41,680
Faut relever le menton.
Chin up.

603
00:28:41,900 --> 00:28:43,120
Et surtout, il faut aller te coucher.
And most importantly, you need to go to bed.

604
00:28:43,920 --> 00:28:45,460
Ta mère a raison, tu dois aller te coucher.
Your mother's right, you should go to bed.

605
00:28:47,450 --> 00:28:48,290
Bonne soirée, Annick.
Good night, Annick.

606
00:28:48,590 --> 00:28:49,330
Pardon de te déranger.
Sorry to bother you.

607
00:28:49,610 --> 00:28:50,650
Non, non, mais ça va, ça va.
No, no, it's fine, it's fine.

608
00:28:51,350 --> 00:28:52,710
Surtout si c'est pour dire que j'ai raison,
Especially if it's to say I'm right —

609
00:28:52,790 --> 00:28:53,530
alors là, t'es pardonnée.
then you're forgiven.

610
00:28:56,410 --> 00:28:59,050
Bon, elle va y arriver, non ? Qu'est-ce que tu en penses, toi ?
She's going to make it, right? What do you think?

611
00:28:59,050 --> 00:29:00,810
Elle est pas en train de souffrir pour rien, là.
She's not going through all this for nothing.

612
00:29:01,530 --> 00:29:02,210
Non, parce que si tu veux,
No, because if you ask me,

613
00:29:02,230 --> 00:29:03,330
si tu penses qu'elle a pas ce qu'il faut,
if you think she doesn't have what it takes,

614
00:29:03,390 --> 00:29:04,610
il vaut mieux le lui dire tout de suite,
it's better to tell her now,

615
00:29:04,670 --> 00:29:08,450
comme ça, au moins, elle finira pas en burn-out, là,
that way at least she won't end up burnt out

616
00:29:08,510 --> 00:29:10,310
comme tous ces parisiens hystériques.
like all those hysterical Parisians.

617
00:29:10,570 --> 00:29:13,230
Bon, écoute, elle a beaucoup des qualités qu'il faut
Look, she has a lot of the qualities you need

618
00:29:13,230 --> 00:29:13,970
pour faire un bon agent.
to be a good agent.

619
00:29:14,590 --> 00:29:16,010
Elle est fine, elle a de l'instinct,
She's sharp, she has instincts,

620
00:29:16,070 --> 00:29:17,410
elle est pugnace, elle est courageuse.
she's tenacious, she's brave.

621
00:29:17,550 --> 00:29:18,190
Je sens venir le mais.
I can feel a "but" coming.

622
00:29:18,930 --> 00:29:20,590
Mais elle manque encore de confiance en elle.
But she still lacks confidence in herself.

623
00:29:20,690 --> 00:29:21,510
OK, OK, OK, stop.
OK, OK, OK, stop.

624
00:29:22,090 --> 00:29:23,470
Il faut arrêter de faire ça.
You have to stop doing that.

625
00:29:23,990 --> 00:29:25,090
Parler de moi comme si j'étais pas là.
Talking about me like I'm not here.

626
00:29:25,270 --> 00:29:26,970
Puis c'est quoi, cette fausse séance de psy ?
And what is this, some fake therapy session?

627
00:29:27,830 --> 00:29:28,970
Camille, écoute ton père.
Camille, listen to your father.

628
00:29:29,070 --> 00:29:30,930
Pour une fois qu'il fait avancer le schmilblick...
For once he's actually moving things forward...

629
00:29:31,330 --> 00:29:31,650
Merci.
Thank you.

630
00:29:33,110 --> 00:29:34,290
Tu sais ce que disait Samuel ?
You know what Samuel used to say?

631
00:29:35,050 --> 00:29:37,150
Ne laisse pas un acteur croire que t'as besoin de lui,
Never let an actor think you need them —

632
00:29:37,230 --> 00:29:38,950
mais toi, fais-lui croire qu'il a besoin de toi.
make them think they need you.

633
00:29:50,130 --> 00:29:51,150
Oh, putain !
Oh, damn!

634
00:29:54,530 --> 00:29:56,250
Elle a fait péter, ta mère !
Your mom came through!

635
00:29:56,610 --> 00:29:58,110
Moi qui l'ai trouvée un petit peu radine.
And I thought she was a little stingy.

636
00:29:58,610 --> 00:29:59,930
C'est pas ma mère, c'est Hicham.
That's not my mom, that's Hicham.

637
00:30:00,760 --> 00:30:01,840
Il a laissé ça au ciel.
He left this for her.

638
00:30:03,030 --> 00:30:04,510
Pour que la petite puce fasse de beaux rêves.
So the little one has sweet dreams.

639
00:30:06,360 --> 00:30:06,920
Oh, non...
Oh, no...

640
00:30:06,920 --> 00:30:07,920
On peut pas s'en empêcher, hein.
We can't help ourselves, can we.

641
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:08,820
Ça creusait dans notre vie.
It was eating away at our lives.

642
00:30:09,400 --> 00:30:11,200
Ah, attends, c'est plus maladroit qu'autre chose.
Look, it's more awkward than anything else.

643
00:30:11,920 --> 00:30:14,460
Puis, franchement, pas mal, le berceau.
And honestly, not a bad crib.

644
00:30:15,380 --> 00:30:16,420
Toi aussi, tu le laisses faire.
You let him do it too.

645
00:30:17,000 --> 00:30:18,000
C'est toi aussi qui est pas claire.
You're not being straight either.

646
00:30:18,360 --> 00:30:19,980
Arrête, je passe mon temps à te tenir à distance.
Stop it, I spend all my time keeping him at a distance.

647
00:30:20,780 --> 00:30:21,480
On dirait pas.
Doesn't look like it.

648
00:30:21,920 --> 00:30:24,520
Parce que je te raconte pas toutes les interactions que j'ai avec lui, si tu veux.
Because I don't tell you about every interaction I have with him, you know.

649
00:30:26,950 --> 00:30:28,510
Mais reste pas comme ça devant le frigo ouvert.
But don't just stand there with the fridge open.

650
00:30:29,330 --> 00:30:30,410
Y a plus de gâteaux ?
Are there no more cakes?

651
00:30:30,410 --> 00:30:31,390
Tu les as finis ?
You finished them?

652
00:30:31,390 --> 00:30:32,650
Bah oui, t'étais pas là pour dîner.
Well yeah, you weren't here for dinner.

653
00:30:34,300 --> 00:30:34,960
Attends, c'est dingue.
Wait, this is unbelievable.

654
00:30:35,100 --> 00:30:36,200
Tu m'en veux, là, en fait ?
Are you actually mad at me right now?

655
00:30:36,200 --> 00:30:39,910
Qui a tellement insisté pour qu'on le garde, ce bébé ?
Who pushed so hard to keep this baby?

656
00:30:39,910 --> 00:30:41,730
Tu le savais que ce serait compliqué avec Hicham.
You knew it would be complicated with Hicham.

657
00:30:41,790 --> 00:30:43,750
On en a parlé pendant des heures. T'as voulu le garder, quand même.
We talked about it for hours. You wanted to keep it anyway.

658
00:30:43,990 --> 00:30:44,610
Ouais, c'est ça.
Yeah, right.

659
00:30:45,150 --> 00:30:47,010
Et c'est moi qui t'ai forcée à tomber enceinte de lui, aussi.
And I suppose I forced you to get pregnant by him too.

660
00:30:48,430 --> 00:30:50,250
En fait, t'en avais rien à foutre des conséquences pour moi.
You just didn't care about what it would mean for me.

661
00:30:50,350 --> 00:30:52,270
T'en avais rien à foutre que je perde mon boulot à New York.
You didn't give a damn that I lost my job in New York.

662
00:30:52,390 --> 00:30:54,610
T'en avais rien à foutre que je me tape sa gueule tous les jours au boulot.
You didn't give a damn that I had to see his face every day at work.

663
00:30:54,710 --> 00:30:56,390
Que je devienne obèse, lourdement handicapée.
That I'd become obese, severely disabled.

664
00:30:56,450 --> 00:30:58,910
Parce que, de toute façon, la seule chose qui t'intéresse vraiment chez moi, c'est ce bébé.
Because, at the end of the day, the only thing you actually care about is this baby.

665
00:30:59,010 --> 00:31:04,710
Alors, c'est dégueulasse de me dire ça.
So it's disgusting of you to say that to me.

666
00:31:05,070 --> 00:31:19,450
Je suis heureuse de le faire.
I'm happy to do it.

667
00:31:19,530 --> 00:31:26,330
Le truc le plus fou que j'ai jamais fait de ma vie, c'est grâce à toi.
The craziest thing I've ever done in my life — I owe that to you.

668
00:31:42,480 --> 00:31:44,500
C'est juste que j'arrête pas d'y penser. Ça m'obsède, en fait.
It's just that I can't stop thinking about it. It's actually obsessing me.

669
00:31:45,080 --> 00:31:46,540
Pourquoi t'as couché avec lui ?
Why did you sleep with him?

670
00:31:49,200 --> 00:31:50,880
J'étais bourrée. J'avais bu trop de champagne.
I was drunk. I'd had way too much champagne.

671
00:31:51,220 --> 00:31:53,880
Mais tu couches pas avec un mec à chaque fois que tu bois trop de champagne ?
But you don't sleep with a guy every time you drink too much champagne?

672
00:31:54,240 --> 00:31:56,200
C'est un champagne hyper hétéro, aussi.
It's a very straight champagne, too.

673
00:31:58,820 --> 00:32:00,520
J'ai besoin de savoir ce qui s'est passé dans ta tête.
I need to know what was going through your head.

674
00:32:01,320 --> 00:32:03,000
Coucher avec un mec, c'est atroce. Je comprends pas.
Sleeping with a guy — it's awful. I don't get it.

675
00:32:03,060 --> 00:32:04,120
Et quand je comprends pas, je m'énerve.
And when I don't get something, I get angry.

676
00:32:05,380 --> 00:32:07,220
Parce que si je comprenais, j'aurais très de temps à vouloir.
Because if I understood, I'd have much less reason to want to.

677
00:32:07,600 --> 00:32:13,090
C'est pas facile à expliquer.
It's not easy to explain.

678
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:17,370
Bon, donc, au début, j'ai été attirée par cette fille.
OK, so, at first, I was attracted to this girl.

679
00:32:18,190 --> 00:32:20,270
Et donc, lui, il l'a emballée sous mon nez.
And then he swept her off her feet right in front of me.

680
00:32:20,370 --> 00:32:23,030
Et ça, ça m'a énervée. Qu'il le fasse et puis qu'elle marche.
And that pissed me off. That he did it and that she went for it.

681
00:32:23,030 --> 00:32:23,930
En plus, c'est de connes.
On top of that, they're idiots.

682
00:32:24,370 --> 00:32:27,630
Bon, donc, voilà. Donc, après, on s'est retrouvées tous les trois.
OK, so anyway. Then the three of us ended up together.

683
00:32:28,370 --> 00:32:30,270
Et en fait, la fille, je la sentais plus trop.
And actually, I wasn't really feeling the girl anymore.

684
00:32:30,870 --> 00:32:32,290
Je sais pas, je la trouvais arrogante.
I don't know, I found her arrogant.

685
00:32:34,390 --> 00:32:36,070
Et c'est avec lui que c'est devenu électrique.
And it was with him that it became electric.

686
00:32:37,370 --> 00:32:39,650
Et enfin, tu vois, ça m'était pas arrivé depuis tellement longtemps.
And I mean, you know, it hadn't happened to me in so long.

687
00:32:39,770 --> 00:32:41,110
Je me rappelais même plus comment c'était.
I'd even forgotten what it felt like.

688
00:32:43,120 --> 00:32:45,300
Et c'était brutal. C'était...
And it was intense. It was...

689
00:32:45,680 --> 00:32:48,260
Enfin, tu vois, j'avais envie de... J'avais envie de le taper.
I mean, you know, I wanted to... I wanted to hit him.

690
00:32:49,280 --> 00:32:50,400
J'avais envie de le dominer.
I wanted to dominate him.

691
00:32:50,620 --> 00:32:52,340
En fait, j'avais vraiment envie de me le faire, tu vois.
I just really wanted to have him, you know.

692
00:32:56,290 --> 00:32:58,150
Arrête, parce que tu visualises, là.
Stop, because you're picturing it right now.

693
00:33:00,120 --> 00:33:01,680
Tu vois, j'aurais pas dû te raconter.
See, I shouldn't have told you.

694
00:33:02,700 --> 00:33:04,360
Oh, maintenant, tu me détestes encore plus.
Oh, now you hate me even more.

695
00:33:13,570 --> 00:33:15,150
On vient vraiment pas de la même planète, toutes les deux.
We really aren't from the same planet, the two of us.

696
00:33:15,590 --> 00:33:19,640
Mais même si ça me fait mal, dis ça aussi que j'aime chez toi.
But even if it hurts me, that's also something I love about you.

697
00:33:19,940 --> 00:33:42,520
C'est juste que ton rendez-vous est arrivé.
It's just that your appointment is here.

698
00:33:42,720 --> 00:33:44,280
C'est un jeune comédien, Brian Vallès.
He's a young actor, Brian Vallès.

699
00:33:44,580 --> 00:33:46,960
OK, OK, j'arrive. Je suis là.
OK, OK, I'm coming. I'm here.

700
00:33:54,220 --> 00:33:56,040
Bonjour, Brian. Camille Valentini.
Hello, Brian. Camille Valentini.

701
00:33:56,640 --> 00:33:56,960
Bonjour.
Hello.

702
00:33:57,140 --> 00:33:58,280
Vous allez bien ? Très bien, merci.
How are you? Very well, thank you.

703
00:33:58,440 --> 00:34:00,340
Excusez-moi, j'étais en pleine négociation.
Excuse me, I was in the middle of a negotiation.

704
00:34:01,270 --> 00:34:02,090
Vous me suivez ?
Would you follow me?

705
00:34:03,180 --> 00:34:04,600
On va se mettre dans la...
We'll go to the...

706
00:34:04,960 --> 00:34:07,600
On va se mettre dans mon bureau.
We'll go to my office.

707
00:34:13,160 --> 00:34:13,720
Beau bureau.
Nice office.

708
00:34:14,320 --> 00:34:14,640
Merci.
Thank you.

709
00:34:19,230 --> 00:34:21,150
Alors, qu'est-ce qui vous amène, Brian ?
So, what brings you in, Brian?

710
00:34:23,970 --> 00:34:26,870
Je sais pas. C'est vous qui avez sollicité ce rendez-vous, donc...
I'm not sure. You're the one who requested this meeting, so...

711
00:34:27,750 --> 00:34:28,430
Oui, évidemment.
Yes, of course.

712
00:34:29,710 --> 00:34:32,490
Parlons un peu de cette belle carrière qui se profile à l'horizon.
Let's talk a little about this promising career on the horizon.

713
00:34:33,780 --> 00:34:36,180
Moi, comme je vous ai déjà dit, j'ai déjà un agent.
As I already told you, I already have an agent.

714
00:34:36,360 --> 00:34:39,260
Mais je trouve que c'est important de rencontrer de nouvelles personnes.
But I think it's important to meet new people.

715
00:34:39,660 --> 00:34:40,380
On sait jamais.
You never know.

716
00:34:41,050 --> 00:34:42,730
Et puis, ASK, c'est quand même une grande agence.
And ASK is a major agency, after all.

717
00:34:42,850 --> 00:34:44,570
Donc, c'est intéressant de voir comment vous travaillez.
So it's interesting to see how you work.

718
00:34:44,810 --> 00:34:45,470
Salut, Mathias.
Hey, Mathias.

719
00:34:48,030 --> 00:34:51,330
Je vous présente mon collègue et ami Mathias Barneville.
Let me introduce my colleague and friend Mathias Barneville.

720
00:34:52,990 --> 00:34:53,270
Bonjour.
Hello.

721
00:34:53,530 --> 00:34:53,910
Bonjour, monsieur.
Good morning, sir.

722
00:34:57,630 --> 00:34:58,870
T'as besoin de quelque chose ?
You need something?

723
00:34:58,870 --> 00:34:59,690
Non, non, non, non.
No, no, no, no.

724
00:34:59,690 --> 00:35:00,210
C'est Iran.
It's Iran.

725
00:35:00,290 --> 00:35:01,350
